#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:1
#: 0acdb1bbc1694254862ca88205573032
msgid "GWexpy for GWpy Users"
msgstr "GWpy ユーザーのための GWexpy"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:3
#: 11771f6bea714582916cc4173a436a82
msgid ""
"This page is the **entry point for moving from GWpy to GWexpy**.   It is "
"not intended to be a full API catalog. The goal is to understand, "
"quickly, what still works as-is and where the high-value differences "
"start."
msgstr ""
"このページは **GWpy から GWexpy へ移行するための入口** です。完全な API "
"カタログを目指すものではありません。目的は、何がそのまま使えて、価値の高い差分がどこから始まるのかを手早く把握することです。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:6
#: d618590e2fec443b9a4c63728b426295
msgid ""
"If you want a **difference-oriented index of added APIs**, see [GWpy "
"Difference API Index](../reference/gwpy_added_api.md).   If you want the "
"full API surface regardless of GWpy compatibility, use the [API "
"Reference](../reference/index.md)."
msgstr ""
"**追加 API を差分観点で引ける一覧** が欲しい場合は [GWpy 差分 API "
"一覧](../reference/gwpy_added_api.md) を参照してください。GWpy 互換性に関係なく全 API を見たい場合は "
"[API リファレンス](../reference/index.md) を使ってください。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:9
#: 7e95568c839d413e91720ff305b80a11
msgid "What to lock in first"
msgstr "まず最初に押さえること"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:11
#: 252177d7c00b4bf89fbfe00866a5079e
msgid ""
"**Single-channel workflows are often still familiar.** For `TimeSeries` /"
" `FrequencySeries` / `Spectrogram`, many basic read, plot, and spectral-"
"analysis paths can be tried first by swapping imports to `gwexpy`."
msgstr ""
"**単一チャンネルのワークフローは、多くの場合これまで通りです。** `TimeSeries` / `FrequencySeries` / "
"`Spectrogram` では、基本的な読み込み・プロット・スペクトル解析の多くが、import を `gwexpy` "
"に差し替えるだけでまず試せます。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:13
#: ba556afc0de84f619eed488cda8cb9a6
msgid ""
"**The biggest shift is multi-channel processing.** Instead of manually "
"looping over `TimeSeriesDict`, you can convert it with `to_matrix()` and "
"treat the channel set as a batch-analysis container."
msgstr ""
"**最も大きく変わるのは多チャンネル処理です。** `TimeSeriesDict` を手動でループする代わりに、`to_matrix()` "
"で変換し、チャンネル群をバッチ解析コンテナとして扱えます。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:15
#: eaeab19abfed487197c5a834d51deebe
msgid ""
"**The Field API is a GWexpy-only extension.** `ScalarField` and "
"`FieldList` / `FieldDict` cover spatially indexed data and batch "
"operations across multiple fields, which GWpy does not provide as a "
"standard layer."
msgstr ""
"**Field API は GWexpy 独自の拡張です。** `ScalarField` や `FieldList` / `FieldDict`"
" は、空間的にインデックス付けされたデータや、複数フィールドにまたがるバッチ操作を扱います。これらは GWpy "
"が標準層として提供していないものです。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:17
#: d9ebc026b3754baa8b3755ea14da26ac
msgid ""
"**Some external-library calls move onto the data object itself.** "
"Representative examples are `.find_peaks()`, `.fit()`, `.hht()`, and "
"`.arima()`."
msgstr ""
"**一部の外部ライブラリ呼び出しは、データオブジェクト自身のメソッドになります。** 代表例は "
"`.find_peaks()`、`.fit()`、`.hht()`、`.arima()` です。"

#: ../../home/washimi/work/gwexpy/docs_redesign/explanation/gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md:19
#: c76185e9471f42b68c7e6072570025a5
msgid ""
"**Direct I/O and interop have their own guides.** Treat [File I/O "
"Supported Formats Guide](../how-to/io_formats.md) as the source of truth "
"for `read(..., format=...)` / `write(..., format=...)`, and [Interop / "
"Conversion Guide](../how-to/interop.md) as the source of truth for "
"`to_*()` / `from_*()` conversions."
msgstr ""
"**直接 I/O と相互運用には専用ガイドがあります。** `read(..., format=...)` / `write(..., "
"format=...)` は [ファイル I/O 対応フォーマットガイド](../how-to/io_formats.md) を、`to_*()`"
" / `from_*()` 変換は [Interop / 変換ガイド](../how-to/interop.md) "
"を、それぞれ一次情報源として参照してください。"

